Timothy C. May says:
> Second, Perry and Harry are consciously pushing the system in various ways
> to try to improve the List. This is mostly their business.

Its not "their" system. Its Harry's. I'm not happy with it. I think
that Harry is too slow to render judgements and makes them overly
technical and long. Harry's a good friend, and it pains me to say
this, but I don't think everyone is cut out to be a judge. I believe
the problem is not in the system but in its execution.

Charges should be considered within hours, not within weeks, of
filing. I've pushed charges weeks ago that STILL haven't been
considered. Unless judgements happen fast, they will not work as a
deterrent to bad posts.

Judgements should be short, of the form "Joe called Fred an asshole.
Any reasonable person would consider this to be an insult. Joe can't
post for a week." Maybe a paragraph more or two if needed. We don't
need four page judgements that can't be read and aren't even clear on
their meaning.

The rules should be followed in their spirit, not according to silly
arbitrary letter. The point is that people should be stopped from
flaming or insulting people, from pushing topics that don't belong,
and for violating the miscelaneous rules concerning not reposting
things from the list. Technicalities and selective enforcement are
BAD, they cause disrespect for the rules.

Lastly, the list intro which states the rules is badly written. It
could explain everything in two paragraphs, sort of like this...

  The Extropians list is designed to encourage free and open
  discussion of Extropian ideas. In order to make sure that this
  discussion can occur free of flame wars and without people having
  worries about their privacy, we ask that you post only on extropian
  topics on this list, that you not attempt to debate list basics, and
  that you avoid insulting others or otherwise flaming. We also ask
  that you never repost anything you see on the extropians list to
  other lists, newsgroups, BBSes, etc.

  Following these simple rules will keep our discussions high-quality
  and allow people to post things like unpublished research papers to
  the list that they do not want in general circulation. If you fail
  to follow these rules, people may ask the list adjudicator to
  penalize you or kick you off the list. If you feel that someone else
  has violated these rules to your detriment, please contact the list
  adjudicator.

